Hand-verified the arithmetic independently against balance.go's BalanceAt/
dayOf: asOfUTC = 2026-09-01 11:00 UTC -> atDay = 2026-09-01 00:00 UTC (UTC
Location, since dayOf rebuilds in `at`'s own Location and asOfUTC's Location
is UTC). txDay for the 05:00 UTC transaction is also 2026-09-01 00:00 UTC.
txDay.After(anchorDay) is true (Sept > Aug 1 anchor) and !txDay.After(atDay)
is true (equal, not after) -> transaction counted -> 1000.00 - 300.00 =
700.00. Confirms 700.00 is correct, not a repeat of the earlier
wrong-fixture incident. Under the mutation, atDay shifts to
2026-08-31 15:00 UTC (JST-derived), the same txDay is now strictly after it,
so the transaction is wrongly excluded -> 1000.00, matching the observed
mutant output exactly.

Not just a "Minimum coincidence": the fixture has zero recurring items, so
byDay is empty and balance is flat across the whole 35-day walk — Minimum is
mathematically forced to equal the starting balance exactly. There is no
alternate path by which Minimum could land on 700.00 without the starting
balance itself being 700.00.

No dependency on projectionHorizonDays or the monthly interval: the fixture
has no recurring items at all, so those constants are irrelevant to this
test.

